#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:490
msgid "Nim the Peddler"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:495
msgid "Psst! Keywright! Nim's pack is full of things that came out of chests and never went back in. Have a look."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:496
msgid "Back again! Nim kept the good ones for you. Well. Nim kept some ones for you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:497
msgid "Quick, before the Guild's men come round the corner. Look, look, but don't point."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:498
msgid "Out of a wizard's strongroom, these. The wizard won't miss them. Nim checked."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:503
msgid "Good eye. Nim would have kept that one, if Nim were the keeping sort."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:504
msgid "Done! Treat it kindly. It's older than the Guild."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:505
msgid "It likes you. Nim can always tell when they like someone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:508
msgid "Nim's off. Two days, three. Nim comes when Nim comes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:508
msgid "Mind the Guild, Keywright. Nim always does."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:511
msgid "That would leave your purse thin, that would. Still want it?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:514
msgid "Not to your taste? Nim has more. Nim always has more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Curios.cs:517
msgid "Back in the pack it goes. Half what you paid: Nim's fair, ask anyone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:72
msgid "Fair Day"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:72
msgid "The whole county's in town for the fair: three more customers today."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:73
msgid "Locking Day"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:73
msgid "Three hundred years since the Locking, and everyone's celebrating: everything sells for a quarter more today."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:74
msgid "The Crown's Buyer"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:74
msgid "The Crown's buyer is in town, paying double for {kind} today."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:75
msgid "A Royal Chest"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:75
msgid "Someone's bringing in one of King Aldric's own chests, gilded, with the royal seal. They think the gold is paint."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:76 scripts/Core/Events.cs:205
msgid "The Stranger"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:76
msgid "A stranger in black is coming by with a chest wrapped in iron chains. Nothing in it can rattle."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:77
msgid "A Storm"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:77
msgid "Few will brave the rain, but those who do bring their best: chests come in a colour better."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:78
msgid "A Barge Aground"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:78
msgid "A treasure barge ran aground on the Aldwater: today's lots come in twos and threes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:79
msgid "A Foreclosure Sale"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:79
msgid "The Guild has foreclosed on a manor, and its chests are being sold off quick: everyone asks a fifth less today."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:80
msgid "The Tourney"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:80
msgid "Knights from four counties are in town for the tourney: weapons and cloaks sell for half again as much today."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:81
msgid "A Day of Mourning"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:81
msgid "The old Duke is being buried, and the whole town's in black. Nobody will stand for a hard shake today."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:82
msgid "The Town Crier"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:82
msgid "Old Lord Harrow lost his family's {kind} to the Locking. His crier offers a reward for one today: three times its price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:83
msgid "The Minstrels' Fair"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:83
msgid "Minstrels are trading songs in the square, and anyone with a box that hums has brought it: a Heartsong is three times as likely today."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:84
msgid "The Sleepers' Moon"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:84
msgid "The Old Wood's moon was full, and all who slept under it dreamt true, like Mother Bramble: every seller tells you their dream. Some warded something."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:85
msgid "Wardens' Day"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:85
msgid "The old custom: ward a keepsake into a chest before you sell it, and leave a riddle for it. Name the answer, and the ward gives it up."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:86 scripts/Core/Events.cs:114
msgid "The Guild's Count"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:86
msgid "The Gilded Guild is counting everything that changes hands: a clerk tallies every article in every chest today, false bottoms and all."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:87
msgid "The Guild's Assessor"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:87
msgid "A Guild assessor sits in the corner all day, and takes a tenth of every sale for the Guild."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:88
msgid "A Witchlight Moon"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:88
msgid "Under a witchlight moon the old enchantments wake: things in today's chests are far likelier to be enchanted."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:100
msgid "Fair Day: +3 customers"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:101
msgid "Locking Day: sales +25%"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:102
#, csharp-format
msgid "Crown buys {0} x2"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:103
msgid "A royal chest today"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:104
msgid "The Stranger's in town"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:105
msgid "Storm: better chests"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:106
msgid "Barge aground: pairs"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:107
msgid "Foreclosure sale: -20%"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:108
msgid "Tourney: arms, cloaks"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:109
msgid "Mourning: no hard shake"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:110
#, csharp-format
msgid "Crier wants {0}"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:111
msgid "Minstrels: songs x3"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:112
msgid "Sleepers' Moon: dreams"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:113
msgid "Wardens' Day: riddles"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:115
msgid "Assessor: sales -10%"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:116
msgid "Witchlight: more magic"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:205
msgid "Stranger"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:207
msgid "A stranger in black who sells chests wrapped tight in iron chains, and never says where they're from. Nothing inside can move, so nothing rattles: all you can learn is how heavy it is, and heavy ones hold more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:209
msgid "Chained tight. No rattles, and no questions. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:209
msgid "Where's it from? Somewhere that wanted it kept shut. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:210
msgid "Some chests are better left shut. Not this one. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:211
msgid "Wise."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:211
msgid "We'll meet again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:212
msgid "Another time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:213
msgid "As you like."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:213
msgid "Someone else, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:214
msgid "Careful."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:214
msgid "It won't open for that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Events.cs:215
msgid "Careful. That will cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:51
msgid "Mister Vane"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:56
msgid "Good evening. The Guild's tithe, if you please. In gold: the Guild has no use for promises."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:57
msgid "Still here, I see. Good. The Guild hates to see a Keywright go to waste."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:58
msgid "I hear you've opened a great many chests this week. The Guild approves. Do keep opening them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:59
msgid "My masters have begun to ask about you. That is rarely good news. One more week after this one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:60
msgid "The last of Bram's debt. Every coin of it, mind. Gold you can see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:65
msgid "Debts are curious things, Keywright. They grow while nobody's watching them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:66
msgid "The Gate is hungry this week, and the Guild has decided you owe it something for its patience."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:67
msgid "Interest, you understand. Nothing personal. My master is very fond of interest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:74
msgid "Paid in full. The Guild has no further claim on Bram's stall. For now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:75
msgid "Paid. Until next week, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:76
msgid "Paid, and promptly. Until next week, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:79
msgid "Short? Then the Guild will take what's on your shelf instead. At the Guild's price, naturally."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:81
msgid "Not enough. The Guild seals this shop tonight, and your licence with it. Your uncle will be so disappointed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:84
msgid "A Guild note, older than the Locking? ...However did you come by that? The Guild honours its own paper. Paid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:87
msgid "All of it, tonight? ...How very thorough of you. The Guild has no further claim on Bram's stall."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:90
msgid "Bram's word? How touching. One week, then. The rest comes due next week, and half as much again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:80
msgid "The Lullaby Box"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:80
msgid "a farmer's wife at Brindle"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:81
msgid "She gave the music box that sang her children to sleep. It still plays her lullaby, for a Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:82
msgid "Calms every seller: nobody hurries you or minds what you do with their chest, and all ask a fifth less."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:83
msgid "The Shepherd's Pipe"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:83
msgid "a shepherd of the Brindle hills"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:84
msgid "He gave the pipe whose tune could call any flock home. It still calls."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:85
msgid "Calls folk to your door: two more customers a day, and anyone who walks out comes back at their first price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:86
msgid "The Fey Chimes"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:86
msgid "the fair folk of the Old Wood"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:87
msgid "They gave the chimes from over their door between the worlds. Where they ring, luck turns."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:88
msgid "Fey luck: a third of what comes out as its chest promised comes out a step better."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:89
msgid "The Dragon's Egg"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:89
msgid "Ysolt, the last dragon of the Ember Peaks"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:90
msgid "She gave her egg, still warm. Three hundred years on, its heart still beats."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:91
msgid "Dragon-gold: coin and gems you sell fetch twice their worth."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:92
msgid "The Clockwork Lark"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:92
msgid "a tinker of Crownhold"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:93
msgid "He gave the bird he built for a princess who never woke. It sings at dawn, and carries word."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:94
msgid "Carries word across Aldmark: two more commissions a week, and every commission pays half as much again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:95
msgid "The Hearthstone"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:95
msgid "the dwarves of Ironroot"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:96
msgid "They gave a stone from their first hearth. It hums with three thousand years of warm evenings."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:97
#, csharp-format
msgid "Folk come for miles to sit by it: {0}g a night for each point of exhibition (more in a grander shop)."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:98
msgid "The Drowned Bell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:98
msgid "old Aldwater, before the river took it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:99
msgid "The town gave its chapel bell, which rang the hours for every soul in Aldwater. It still counts, under the water."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:100
msgid "It counts for you: as a chest comes to the counter, it tolls once for each thing inside, false bottom and all."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:101
msgid "The Bottled Star"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:101
msgid "the archmages of the Keyhold"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:102
msgid "They gave a star they caught as students and kept in a bottle all their lives. Things from the Locking gather round it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:103
msgid "Starlight: enchanted things glow whenever they sound, witchlight or not, and turn up far more often."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:104
msgid "The Imp's Ember"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:104
msgid "Pib, an imp who loved a miller's daughter"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:105
msgid "He gave his own heart, a coal that never goes out, so the Maw could never have her."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:106
msgid "Tempers all it warms: glass never breaks, nothing comes out worse than promised, and fakes you open burn true."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:114
msgid "A lock of gold could never hold the demon of greed. So at the Locking the archmages asked the peoples of Aldmark for things they loved more than gold, and sang the Locking into nine of them: the Heartsongs. Then they hid each in an ordinary chest, among millions. Only a Keywright hears one sing. To anyone else it's worth nothing, and the Guild won't touch one: greed can't put a price on it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:11
msgid "Uncle Bram"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:16
msgid "Morning! Here's the trick of it: a chest opens for you once you've paid for it, and nobody can see inside, so everyone shakes it and guesses. Tam never even shook his. Drag the chest slowly from side to side: that's a gentle shake."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:19
msgid "Your back won't take a hard shake or a drop, Hesk, but your scale doesn't lie. Weigh what you heard against what's on the scale: whatever's left over is something you couldn't hear, or something under a false bottom."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:21
msgid "Everybody haggles with you, Rosa, though they open a bit higher, knowing you. Make your offer with the slider. Too low and they'll let you try again, but walk one out of the door and they won't be back this week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:23
msgid "Your shelf's up from the first day, Isolde. Keep what you love: visitors pay at the door every night, a coin for every point of exhibition. Just remember the Guild won't take your collection in pawn on a short night."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:25
msgid "Hear that jingle? Coin. Light things rattle at the gentlest shake. Tick Coin on your slip, there on the right."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:26
msgid "Your slip adds up what you've ticked, valued as good as the chest's colour promises. The bar underneath is your odds that it's worth more than the price: the greener, the safer."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:28
msgid "Penn only shook it gently. Nothing heavy or soft stirs for a gentle shake, so she's priced only what she heard. Try every strength yourself: gentle, firm and hard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:30
msgid "That flump is a cloak. Soft things only make a sound when you shake hard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:31
msgid "Hob shook it hard, and when something clanks, it drowns out anything delicate. Shake it yourself, at every strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:32
msgid "Clank: a weapon, an axe or a blade. It only moves when you shake firmly, and while it's clanking you can't hear anything delicate. Shake gently to hear past it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:34
msgid "Mags counts the rattles at a firm shake and charges the same for each. If you can't hear anything she didn't, pass: a seller always asks a bit more than what they've heard is worth."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:36
msgid "When you pass, they take it home unopened, and you'll never know for sure. But your gut usually has an opinion."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:37
msgid "A tick is a good read. A cross is something to listen for next time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:38
#, csharp-format
msgid "That's a day's trading. Every coin goes toward the stall: once it's earned {0}g, all told, we'll talk about Thornwick."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:41
msgid "Look at the chest's colour: plain wood, green, blue, purple. The Wardens painted them by what went in, so the colour tells you how good the things inside tend to be. Only tend to: you'll get surprises both ways."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:43
msgid "See? Not everything matches its chest. Mostly it does; sometimes it's a little worse; now and then it's much better."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:44
msgid "This one names a price. Take it or leave it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:45
msgid "This one haggles, so they'll start high. Use the slider to make one offer: they'll take it, name a final price, or storm off if you insult them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:47
msgid "This one wants you to name a price. Offer what it's worth to you, less a little. You get two tries."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:48
msgid "Too low. One more try, then they'll go."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:49
msgid "Everyone you've traded with has a page in your notebook: how they judge a chest, how they trade, what they're like. Click whoever's at the counter to read theirs."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:51
msgid "Listen to where they say it came from. A barrow holds grave goods, a goblin warren mostly coin, a dwarf-hold weapons and gems."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:53
msgid "Something grand? You can keep it for display instead of selling it. A good exhibition brings more customers, and better ones. Enchanted things count double."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:55
msgid "On display. You'll see it on the shelf behind the counter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:56
msgid "Your exhibition. Click anything in it to sell it, if you need the money."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:59
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0}g earned: the stall pays its way! Thornwick Market has more customers, richer chests and room for a shelf. But Thornwick chests cost more, so keep enough for tomorrow's. A price in red means it would leave you short: better to wait a day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:60
msgid "Nearly broke? I keep a little put by for days like this. Don't tell the Guild. It won't last forever: the day card says how much is left."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:62
msgid "A shelf behind the counter, with room for one thing! Keep something grand on display instead of selling it: an exhibition draws more customers, and better chests. Each cabinet you buy makes room for one more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:64
#, csharp-format
msgid "Crownhold folk know a shop by what it collects. Your notebook has tallied everything you've acquired: {0} of a kind earns a synergy. Open Synergies, bottom right, to put one to work or see how close you are."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:65
msgid "Another synergy slot: open Synergies and put one more to work."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:66
msgid "The Royal Emporium, in the palace's shadow. The Gate's just down the street: you can feel it hum. There are bigger things to grow into now: a night market, a patrons' book, a velvet case for curios. Keep enough back for Vane."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:68
msgid "Forgotten a sound, or someone's habits? Press N for your notebook: the sounds, the regulars you've met, and a calendar of what's coming."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:70
msgid "That's the Guild's next due, up top. Click it any time for the whole debt in your notebook: what's paid, what's left, and what each week will want."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:72
msgid "The ward's let go: the chest is yours. Now for the old lock underneath. The pick sweeps round: press {act}, or click, while it's in the green to set a pin. Set every pin cleanly and nothing inside gets scratched."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:76
msgid "Paid. Next week the Guild wants more, and more again the week after. Whatever you spend on the shop has to earn its keep before Vane comes back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:78
msgid "Nim sells curios: oddments from the Locking, each bending one rule of the trade. You've only so much room for them, so pick ones that work together. Nim notices what you buy and brings more like it, and keeps his rarest for a real collector. Don't ask what Nim is."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:81
msgid "The regulars want things now: see the board on the left. When something they want comes out of a chest, hand it over instead of selling it. A commission always pays more than a sale, and a lot pays piece by piece."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:83
msgid "Someone wants this! Deliver it: a commission always pays more than selling it would."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:84
msgid "Something's happening in town today: two days every week are different. It's up in the top bar (click it to read it again), and your notebook's calendar shows what's coming this week and next."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:86
msgid "The Stranger. That chest's wrapped in iron chains: nothing inside can move, so there's nothing to hear. Drop it to feel how heavy it is. Heavy ones hold more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:88
msgid "A royal seal! That's one of King Aldric's own chests, gilded. The seller thinks the gold is paint, and priced it as the colour underneath."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:90
msgid "Look at that purse: enough to pay off the whole back-tithe, every week of it, right now! Do it, and the stall is ours early. Or keep trading first: the Guild only ever asks for this week's."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:92
msgid "Short? Pawn what's on display, or your curios, at the Guild's price. If even that isn't enough, the Guild seals the shop."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:93
msgid "The Hooded Woman pays in shards of the Aldric Key. If you can't find what she wants this week, she'll ask again next week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:96
msgid "Thornwick folk bring two new sounds. Potions slosh at a gentle shake, like coin. Spells (scrolls and spellbooks) rustle only at a hard shake, like cloaks. And some chests are locked, or have a false bottom. It'll be a quiet first day, while word gets round."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:99
msgid "Locked. Buy it and you'll pick the lock before you open it. A crowbar's quicker, but it breaks glass."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:100
msgid "Dropped! A solid thud means a plain chest. A hollow boom means a false bottom: something hidden that nobody's priced."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:101
msgid "Hear that boom? A false bottom. Tick it on your slip: whatever's down there, nobody's priced it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:102
msgid "Glass breaks when you drop it. If you heard a slosh, think twice before dropping."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:103
msgid "That slosh is a potion. It's delicate, like coin: a clank drowns it out."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:104
msgid "A rustle: a spell, a scroll or a spellbook. Soft, like a cloak: it only sounds at a hard shake."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:105
msgid "Crownhold brings gems, which tinkle at a gentle shake; archmages, whose things are often enchanted (a witchlight would show it); and lots with two or three of a kind. Count the rattles: click a row again for each one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:107
msgid "A tinkle: a gem. Delicate, and worth the most."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:108
msgid "The witchlight's lit, and it stays lit: anything enchanted glows when it makes a sound. Click the star on a row to mark one enchanted."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:110
msgid "Two of a kind: each one adds its value. Sellers who don't count only price one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:111
msgid "It glowed! That one's enchanted, and worth twice as much. Click the star on its row to mark it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:112
msgid "The Royal Emporium. Court folk, the Maw's creatures up through the cracks in the Gate, and Silas, who sells demon gold: gilded iron that jingles just like the real thing. A lodestone would catch it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:114
msgid "The lodestone's on, so iron can't move. Weapons go quiet, and nothing drowns out the delicate things. Demon gold, which is iron under the gilt, goes quiet too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:116
msgid "That's all the shaking this one will stand: it's coming apart. Go by what you heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:119
msgid "That sound... I've heard it once in forty years. A Heartsong! Only a Keywright hears one sing, so the seller has no idea it's there. It's worth nothing in gold and everything to the shop: buy that chest. And if you can't afford it, pass: a Heartsong won't leave with them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:122
msgid "A Heartsong. Nobody would pay a penny for one, but each does something for the shop that no gold can, for as long as it sings here. Keep it or let it go: every one you keep makes the next harder to find."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:124
msgid "Hear that? The whole stall's different with it singing. It'll sing as long as it's ours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:128
msgid "Penn only shakes gently, so heavy things and soft things make no sound for her."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:129
msgid "Dorrin's Barrow chests are rotten: about two seconds of shaking, all told. One strength, then: pick it well."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:130
msgid "Snikkit puts his price up a tenth for every strength you try after the first. Pick two: gentle and hard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:131
msgid "Mother Bramble always dreams true, in signs. If you can't hear what she dreamt of, it's warded: name it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:132
msgid "A Thornwick dowry always holds coin, a cloak and a potion. Whichever of the three you can't hear is warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:133
msgid "Wren's tag lists every kind of thing packed. A kind on the tag that never makes a sound is warded: name it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:134
msgid "Quill's ward-roll names the warded thing, faded. Make out the name, and tick its kind."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:135
msgid "Madame Oriel's cards: a suit drawn twice is what the ward holds. Three different suits, and nothing's warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:136
msgid "A warded thing makes no sound and weighs nothing. Name it on your slip, and nothing that isn't there, and the ward will give it up."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:138
msgid "You could pay off the Guild now. Or buy its Bookkeeping Engine for the same sum: it reads every chest for you, to finish the run quickly."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:140
msgid "Wenna's scale says what her chest weighs. Take away the weight of what you heard: what's left never stirred (a cloak is 3 lb, a spell 1)."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:142
msgid "Pell's ticket counts every article, false bottom and all. Count what you hear: one short means one under the floor."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:143
msgid "Brother Ansel won't have his chests shaken hard: half again if you do. Crypt chests are full of holy cloaks."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:144
msgid "Fennick packs his chests in straw: everything needs a strength harder to stir, and cloaks and spells won't stir at all. Shake firmly, then hard, then drop it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:146
msgid "Orrin likes a wager: read his chest exactly, every kind and every count, and he gives back a third of the price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:147
msgid "Solve grandmother's riddle. If you can't hear what it's about, it's warded: name it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:148
msgid "Sir Aldous takes the best weapon in his chest, for the fee he names. Value what's left."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:149
msgid "Vexis gives you twelve seconds. Gently, then hard, and decide."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:150
msgid "Malbranche is cheap, but the dearest thing inside is his. A chest of many middling things suits his bargain."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:151
msgid "Skrae's echoes come back off everything, warded or not. An echo with nothing to hear is warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:152
msgid "Lady Ermine prices only her gems; the rest comes free. Some are paste, and she won't have a lodestone near them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:153
msgid "Old Aldo's price is your slip. Get it exactly right and he takes a quarter off; get it wrong and you pay what it holds, and a quarter more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:155
msgid "The Maw sells for one coin, but everyone who comes after him today asks twice as much. Count who's still waiting."
msgstr ""

