#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:308
msgid "Easy!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:322
msgid "Little Tam"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:322
msgid "Tam"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:325
msgid "I fished it out of the millpond! It's still dripping. Mum says never shake things, so I didn't. What'll you give me?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:326
msgid "It was stuck in the mill wheel. Dad says it's full of frogs. How much will you give me for it?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:327
msgid "It was under Gran's bed. She says I can sell it if I don't tell Mum. What's it worth?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:328
msgid "I found it in our hayloft, behind the cat. The cat didn't want it. How much?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:329
msgid "A village boy who fishes chests out of the millpond and never shakes them: he has no idea what's in one, and asks you to name a price. A few coins will do, but a millpond chest is sometimes empty."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:331
msgid "Yay! I'm buying sweets!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:331
msgid "Really? Thanks, mister!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:332
msgid "Is that all? Um... a bit more?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:332
msgid "Mum says don't take the first offer."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:333
msgid "Aww. I'll ask someone else."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:333
msgid "Never mind. Gran will have it back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:334
msgid "Aww. Okay."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:334
msgid "I'll throw it back, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:335
msgid "Hey! That's MY chest!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:335
msgid "Whoa! Do it again!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:336
msgid "You broke it! Now it costs more!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:340
msgid "Widow Penn"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:340
msgid "Penn"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:343
msgid "My Tobb's old soldiering chest. I only gave it a gentle shake: I couldn't bear to hear his things rattle about. Would {price} do?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:344
msgid "Tobb carried this through two wars, dear. I couldn't bring myself to shake it more than gently. Is {price} fair?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:345
msgid "It was Tobb's mother's, from the attic. Just a gentle shake, dear: my wrists aren't what they were. {price}?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:346
msgid "A soldier's widow selling her husband's things. She only ever shakes a chest gently, so what's heavy (a weapon) or soft (a cloak) never makes a sound for her, and she doesn't price it. A soldier's kitbag usually holds both."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:348
msgid "Thank you, dear. Truly."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:348
msgid "Bless you. Tobb would have liked you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:349
msgid "I'm sorry, dear, I can't stand here all day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:349
msgid "I'll come back when you're less busy."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:350
msgid "That's all right, dear. I'll keep it a while longer."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:350
msgid "Never mind. It was good of you to look."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:351
msgid "Oh! Gently, dear, please."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:351
msgid "Oh my. Those were Tobb's things."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:352
msgid "Those were Tobb's things! I'm sorry, but I'll want more now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:356
msgid "Hob the Farmer"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:356
msgid "Hob"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:358
msgid "Turned up under the plough on the old battlefield. I gave it a good hard shake, like the hay. {price}, and that's a bargain!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:359
msgid "Every spring that field coughs up another one. Shook it like a sack of turnips. Say, {price}?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:360
msgid "A farmer who ploughs chests up out of the old battlefield and shakes them hard, so a clanking weapon drowns out any coin for him. He haggles, and starts at about twice what he'll take."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:362
msgid "Deal! Wait till I tell the missus."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:362
msgid "Done! Easy money."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:363
msgid "Hmm. {price}, and that's my last word."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:363
msgid "The wife'd skin me. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:364
msgid "Daylight robbery! Forget it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:364
msgid "I've cows to milk. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:365
msgid "Your loss. Field's full of them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:365
msgid "Suit yourself. I'll be back after the next ploughing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:366
msgid "Steady on! It's not a sack of spuds."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:366
msgid "Ha! Mind your toes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:367
msgid "Easy with my chest! That'll cost you extra."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:371
msgid "Mags the Innkeeper"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:371
msgid "Mags"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:373
msgid "Some adventurer left this to settle his tab. I gave it a good shake and counted the rattles. So much a rattle, love: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:374
msgid "Three nights' ale and a broken bench, and he paid me in chest. I charge by the rattle, love: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:375
msgid "Keeps the Crossed Keys at the crossroads and takes chests for unpaid tabs. She gives one a firm shake, counts the rattles, and charges the same for each, whatever's rattling: a goblin cleaver costs what a purse of coin does."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:377
msgid "Pleasure doing business!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:377
msgid "Done, love. Come by for a pint."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:378
msgid "I've a taproom to run, love. Another time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:379
msgid "Suit yourself, love. Someone'll have it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:379
msgid "Fair enough. I'll stick it behind the bar."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:380
msgid "Oi! I'll want that back in one piece."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:380
msgid "Mind my floor, love."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:381
msgid "Oi! You break it, you pay for it, love. Half again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:385
msgid "Dorrin the Delver"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:385
msgid "Dorrin"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:387
msgid "Dragged it up from the Barrow's second vault. The damp's got into the wood: go easy, it won't stand much. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:388
msgid "From the Barrow. I lost my torch and my nerve down there, but I kept the chest. It's half rotten. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:389
msgid "I ran from a barrow-wight for this, so it's yours for {price}. Careful: it's falling apart."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:390
msgid "A young adventurer back from the Barrow. Prices a chest by its colour and never shakes it: Barrow chests are so rotten they stand about two seconds of shaking before they start to come apart. Grave goods: coin, weapons, gems."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:392
msgid "Drinks are on me tonight!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:392
msgid "Right. Back to the Barrow!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:393
msgid "Sorry, I've a barrow to get back to."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:394
msgid "Fair enough. Someone at the Crossed Keys will want it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:394
msgid "Oh well. More where that came from."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:395
msgid "Careful, it's rotten!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:395
msgid "Whoa! It'll fall apart!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:396
msgid "It's held together with damp and hope! You'll pay more for that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:402
msgid "Snikkit the Goblin"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:402
msgid "Snikkit"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:404
msgid "From the warren, yes yes. Very shiny. Snikkit shake it gentle, only gentle. {price}. Looking is free. Looking more, not free!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:405
msgid "Snikkit's cousins find it, Snikkit sells it. Gentle shake only. {price}. You want to shake more? You pay more!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:406
msgid "Warren chest. Smells of goblin. Is fine. {price}, and more every time you shake it different."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:407
msgid "Ooh, you like! Price go up: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:407
msgid "More shaking, more gold! {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:407
msgid "Hehe. {price} now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:408
msgid "A goblin selling what his cousins pinch: warren chests, mostly coin. He only shakes gently, so he never prices what a gentle shake can't stir, and goblins charge for everything, looking included: each strength you try after your first puts his price up a tenth."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:411
msgid "Shiny! Shiny!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:411
msgid "Hehehe. Sucker. I mean, friend."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:412
msgid "Pah! Snikkit has other customers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:413
msgid "Pah! Snikkit sell it to someone with eyes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:413
msgid "Your loss. Snikkit's gain. Snikkit always gains."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:414
msgid "Eek! Snikkit's chest!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:414
msgid "Hehe, again! Again!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:415
msgid "You drop Snikkit's chest? Price go up!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:419
msgid "Wenna the Huntress"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:419
msgid "Wenna"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:423
msgid "Took it off an outlaws' camp on the Thornwick road. My game scale says {pounds}. {price}. Go gently: the mare spooks."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:424
msgid "The outlaws won't be needing it. {pounds} on my scale, and I price by the pound: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:425
msgid "Found it in a wolf den. The wolves had eaten whoever was carrying it. {pounds} on my scale. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:426
msgid "Wolves don't hoard, but their dinners did. {pounds}, to the half pound. {price}. Easy with it: the mare."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:427
msgid "A huntress who weighs every chest on her game scale and prices it by the pound, so light things (spells, gems) come cheap. Her chests hang on a mare who bolts at a hard shake, so nobody can shake one hard: take the weight of what you heard from what the scale says, and what's left is what never stirred."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:430
msgid "Good hunting."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:431
msgid "The mare's restless. I'm off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:432
msgid "No matter. It'll sell at the next market."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:432
msgid "Fair enough."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:433
msgid "Easy! You'll have the mare bolting."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:433
msgid "Steady."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:434
msgid "Easy! You've upset the mare, and me. Half again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:438
msgid "Mother Bramble"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:438
msgid "Bramble"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:441
msgid "The Old Wood let this one go. I slept beside it and dreamt of {dream}. The oaks whispered its price: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:442
msgid "Moss grew on it for a hundred years. Last night I dreamt of {dream}, and of a price: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:443
msgid "A druid of the Old Wood. Her price comes to her in a dream, and she always dreams true, in signs: of what the Wood warded in the chest, or else of the dearest thing in it. A magpie is coin, a thorn a weapon, a raven's wing a cloak, a river a potion, an owl a spell, a star a gem. If you can't hear what she dreamt of, it's warded: name it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:446
msgid "As the Wood wills."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:446
msgid "The oaks approve."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:447
msgid "The Wood is calling me home."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:448
msgid "The Wood is patient. So am I."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:448
msgid "Then it wasn't meant for you. Not yet."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:449
msgid "Mind the moss, child."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:449
msgid "The Wood felt that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:450
msgid "The Wood felt that, child. So will your purse."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:454
msgid "Brother Ansel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:454
msgid "Ansel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:456
msgid "From the abbey crypt, by the Abbot's leave. I shook it firmly, but not hard, please: the saints are resting. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:457
msgid "Brother Cuthbert's reliquary. I gave it a firm shake, as is seemly. {price}, for the roof fund."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:458
msgid "A young monk selling the crypt's chests to mend the abbey roof. He shakes a chest firmly and won't have it shaken hard (half again if you do), so the holy cloaks a crypt chest is full of never make a sound for him, and go unpriced."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:460
msgid "Bless you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:460
msgid "The roof thanks you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:461 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:465
msgid "Brother! The saints! Half again, for the sacrilege."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:462
msgid "Forgive me, I'm due at vespers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:463
msgid "Another day, perhaps. The roof can wait. A little."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:463
msgid "Peace be with you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:464
msgid "Brother! Gently!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:464
msgid "Oh! Saint Cuthbert preserve us."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:469
msgid "Fennick the Smuggler"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:469
msgid "Fennick"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:472
msgid "Packed in straw, so nothing clinked at the Wardens' toll. I gave it a firm shake. {price}, and no questions."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:473
msgid "Came up the smugglers' road. Don't ask. The straw muffles everything, but I gave it a firm shake. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:474
msgid "Runs brandy past the Wardens' toll on the forest road, every chest packed in straw so nothing clinks: everything in it needs a strength harder to stir, and cloaks and spells won't stir at all. He gives it a firm shake, never drops it, and smugglers love a false bottom. Haggles."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:477
msgid "Pleasure. We never met."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:477
msgid "Done. Mind the Wardens."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:478
msgid "{price}, and you're robbing me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:478
msgid "Tch. {price}, final."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:479
msgid "Hmph. Plenty of other buyers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:479
msgid "I've a wagon to catch."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:480
msgid "Your loss. I was never here."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:480
msgid "Suit yourself. Forget my face."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:481
msgid "Quiet! Do you want the Wardens round?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:481
msgid "Easy. That's straw, not stone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:482
msgid "Quiet, you fool! That noise will cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:486
msgid "Gerda the Matchmaker"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:486
msgid "Gerda"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:489
msgid "A dowry, love, from a wedding that never was: {clue}, as ever. Shaken hard: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:490
msgid "The groom ran off to the Barrow. Her dowry: {clue}. Shaken hard: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:491
msgid "Thornwick's matchmaker, selling dowries from weddings that never happened. A Thornwick dowry always holds coin for luck, a cloak for warmth and a potion for health, and a bride often wards one of the three: whichever you can't hear is the warded one. Gerda shakes hard and prices what she hears, never what's warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:494
msgid "May it bring you luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:494
msgid "Mind you use it well, love."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:495
msgid "I've a match to make, love. Toodle-oo."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:496
msgid "Ah well. There's always another wedding."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:496
msgid "Not to your taste? Nor was the groom to hers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:497
msgid "Mind the bride's things, love!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:497
msgid "Ooh! Careful."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:498
msgid "That's a bride's dowry, love! It'll cost you more now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:504
msgid "Wren the Apprentice"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:504
msgid "Wren"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:507
msgid "Master Orrin's clearing out the Arcanum stores. The tag says: packed, {clue}. Master says {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:508
msgid "This one's from the third cellar. I can read the tag, at least: {clue}. {price}, Master says."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:509
msgid "An archmage's apprentice clearing out the Arcanum stores. Every chest still has its packing tag, listing each kind of thing packed in it, and the archmages warded the most dangerous: a kind on the tag that you can't hear is warded. Prices by the chest's colour, as his master tells him."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:512
msgid "Oh good! Don't tell Master I was nervous."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:512
msgid "Thank you!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:513
msgid "I'm late! Master will turn me into something."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:514
msgid "Oh. Master won't be pleased."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:514
msgid "That's all right. There's a whole cellar of them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:515
msgid "Careful! Some of those are cursed!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:515
msgid "Eep!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:516
msgid "Master said to keep them in one piece! I'll have to ask more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:520
msgid "Archmage Orrin"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:520
msgid "Orrin"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:522
msgid "I packed this myself, when the Locking was new. {price}. Tell me exactly what's in it, and a third comes back to you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:523
msgid "A {colour} chest from my own stores. {price}. Read it true, Keywright, and I'll return a third. I like to see the craft done well."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:524
msgid "An archmage old enough to remember the Locking. He prices by the chest's colour, and likes a wager: read his chest exactly right, every kind and every count, and he gives back a third of what you paid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:526
msgid "Let us see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:526
msgid "We shall see what you heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:527
msgid "I have three hundred years of reading to catch up on. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:528
msgid "Prudent. Or timid. We shall never know."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:528
msgid "Another time, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:529
msgid "Hm. Bold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:529
msgid "In my day we were gentler with the Locking's work."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:530
msgid "That chest is older than your great-grandmother. A third more, I think."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:534
msgid "Grit the Miner"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:534
msgid "Grit"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:536
msgid "Dug it out of the deep seam under Ironroot. Gave it a hard shake, with dwarf's hands. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:537
msgid "From Ironroot hold, sealed since my great-great-grandmother's day. I gave it a proper shake. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:538
msgid "A dwarf of Ironroot who knows a weapon when he hears one. He prices weapons in full, everything else at half, and takes every tinkle for a diamond. He shakes hard, and haggles."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:540
msgid "Done. Back to the deep."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:540
msgid "Ha! Done."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:541
msgid "{price}. Any lower and I'll eat my helmet."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:541
msgid "{price}, and that's stone-solid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:542
msgid "You take me for a fool? Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:543
msgid "Hmph. Your loss, surface-dweller."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:543
msgid "Back down the mine with it, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:544
msgid "Ha! Dwarf-made. It'll take worse than that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:544
msgid "Watch it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:545
msgid "Mind my stone-work! That'll cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:549
msgid "Lady Corisande"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:549
msgid "Corisande"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:552
msgid "Grandmother's trick box. Her riddle's on the lid: \"{clue}\" {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:553
msgid "From our strongroom: {price}. Grandmother's riddle: \"{clue}\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:554
msgid "A noblewoman selling her grandmother's trick boxes. Each lid has grandmother's riddle about one thing inside, and if she warded something, the riddle is about that. Solve it: if you can't hear the answer, it's warded. Prices by colour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:556
msgid "How delightful."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:556
msgid "Grandmother would approve."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:557
msgid "I have a fitting at four. Do excuse me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:558
msgid "Pity. Grandmother so loved a puzzle."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:558
msgid "Another time, perhaps."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:559
msgid "Goodness!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:559
msgid "Do be careful, that's a de Vere."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:560
msgid "That is a de Vere heirloom! The price has just gone up."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:564
msgid "Pell the Pawnbroker"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:564
msgid "Pell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:567
msgid "Pledged twenty years ago and never redeemed. The ticket says {articles}. I gave it a firm shake. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:568
msgid "Ticket four thousand and twelve: {articles}, it says. I price a lot kind by kind, at a firm shake. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:569
msgid "Sells pawn lots nobody redeemed, often two or three of a kind. He prices one of each kind he hears and never counts how many. The pawn ticket counts every article pledged, false bottom and all, and he won't have pledges dropped: count what you hear against the ticket."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:572
msgid "Done. No refunds."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:572
msgid "Sold, as heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:573 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:577
msgid "Not on my pledges! Half again, for the damage."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:574
msgid "Time is money, and you're spending mine."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:575
msgid "Back on the shelf it goes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:575
msgid "As you like. Pledges keep."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:576
msgid "Mind the pledges!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:581
msgid "Quill the Archivist"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:581
msgid "Quill"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:584
msgid "From the Royal Archive's vaults, with its ward-roll: {clue}. Three hundred years of damp. So much a rattle: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:585
msgid "Unclaimed since the Locking. The ward-roll reads {clue}, as far as I can make it out. I counted the rattles: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:586
msgid "The Royal Archive's clerk, selling unclaimed vault chests with their ward-rolls. A roll names what was warded in its chest, its letters faded by three hundred years: read the name, and name its kind on your slip. A blank roll means nothing was warded. He counts the rattles at a firm shake and charges the same for each."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:589
msgid "Duly recorded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:589
msgid "I'll file the receipt."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:590
msgid "The Archive closes at six. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:591
msgid "Very well. I'll file it under 'unsold'."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:591
msgid "Noted."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:592
msgid "Careful! That's Crown property."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:592
msgid "Oh dear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:593
msgid "That is Crown property! I'll have to add a fee for that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:597
msgid "Shelly the Mudlark"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:597
msgid "Shelly"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:600
msgid "Out of the Aldwater mud at low tide! I shook it hard, and I'd bet my boots on what rustles. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:601
msgid "The river gives and the river takes. Shook it hard: spellbooks, potions, who knows! {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:602
msgid "Combs the Aldwater mud at low tide, shakes hard, and prices every rustle as a drowned wizard's spellbook. Her scroll cases are often full of river sand, which pours at the gentlest shake. Real parchment only rustles at a hard one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:604
msgid "Mud's been good to me!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:604
msgid "The river provides."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:605
msgid "Tide's turning. I'm off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:606
msgid "Back in the barrow, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:606
msgid "No skin off my nose."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:607
msgid "Ha! It's been through worse in the river."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:607
msgid "Oop!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:608
msgid "Oi! Mud or no mud, that's mine. It'll cost more now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:612
msgid "Sir Aldous"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:612
msgid "Aldous"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:614
msgid "Grandfather's war chest. If his sword's in it, it's mine, and I'll pay you {fee} for it. The rest is yours for {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:615
msgid "The de Lacy war chest, from the siege of Harrowgate. Any blade in it is my family's: {fee} for the best. {price} for the chest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:616
msgid "A knight looking for his grandfather's sword. Prices by colour. If there are weapons in his chest, the best of them goes back to him for the price he names: value what's left."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:618
msgid "Honour is satisfied."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:618
msgid "For the de Lacys!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:619
msgid "I'm expected at the lists. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:620
msgid "Then I shall keep looking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:620
msgid "Another chest, another day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:621
msgid "Have a care, sir!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:621
msgid "Steady!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:622
msgid "Have a care with my grandfather's things! It'll cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:628
msgid "Vexis the Imp"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:628
msgid "Vexis"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:631
msgid "Fresh through the Gate, from the Maw's own hoard. {price}. And the sand's already running, mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:632
msgid "Hot off the Gilded Gate. A {colour} chest: {price}. Tick, tock."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:633
msgid "An imp with an hourglass, selling from the Maw's hoard. Prices by colour and never looks inside, and gives you twelve seconds to decide. Things from the Maw's hoard are often better than their chest's colour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:635
msgid "Delicious."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:635
msgid "A pleasure, mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:636
msgid "Too slow! Back through the Gate I go."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:637
msgid "Pfft. Your loss, mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:637
msgid "Fine. Someone in the Emporium has more sense."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:638
msgid "Hee! Again!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:638
msgid "Clumsy mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:639
msgid "Careful, mortal! Breakages cost extra."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:643 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:643
msgid "Malbranche"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:645
msgid "From the Maw's hoard. {price}, a pittance. My only condition: the dearest thing inside is mine."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:646
msgid "A bargain, mortal: {price}. When it opens, I take the best of it. Everything else is yours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:647
msgid "A skeletal devil who deals in bargains. His price is low, but the dearest thing inside is his. A chest of many middling things suits his deal; one grand thing and little else doesn't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:649
msgid "Signed and sealed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:649
msgid "A pleasure doing business. It always is."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:650
msgid "My time is worth more than yours, mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:651
msgid "Another time. There is always another time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:651
msgid "How very wise of you. Or was it?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:652
msgid "Mind my bones."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:652
msgid "Tsk."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:653
msgid "Damaged goods cost more, mortal. Read the small print."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:657 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:657
msgid "Skrae"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:660
msgid "Shaken gently, then hard: {price}. Then I clicked, like a bat. The echoes: {clue}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:661
msgid "I hear every coin in the realm. {price}. My echoes: {clue}. Wards can't stop an echo."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:662
msgid "A demon with ears like a bat. It shakes a chest gently, then hard, and prices what it hears, fairly. Then it clicks and listens to the echoes, which come back off everything inside, warded or not: round is coin, long a weapon, soft a cloak, hollow a potion, flat a spell, tiny a gem. An echo you can't hear is warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:665
msgid "Fair."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:665
msgid "You won't regret it. Probably."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:666
msgid "I hear someone counting gold elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:667
msgid "I heard that coming."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:667
msgid "Hm. Fair enough."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:668
msgid "Ow! My ears!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:668
msgid "Loud. Very loud."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:669
msgid "My ears! That will cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:673
msgid "Lady Ermine"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:673
msgid "Ermine"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:676
msgid "From my strongroom. My gems, and whatever my maid packed. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:677
msgid "The gems alone are worth {price}, I'm told. The rest I couldn't say. My maid packs."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:678
msgid "A lady of the court who knows her own jewels and nothing else: she prices her gems at what she paid for them, and whatever else her maid packed comes free. Some of her gems are paste, and she won't have a lodestone near them (half again if you try)."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:681
msgid "Charming."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:681
msgid "Do look after them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:682
msgid "A lodestone? On MY gems? Half again, for the insult."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:683
msgid "I'm expected at court. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:684
msgid "How very disappointing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:684
msgid "Well. Someone at court will have it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:685
msgid "My gems!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:685
msgid "Must you?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:686
msgid "My gems! Half again, for the fright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:690
msgid "Madame Oriel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:690
msgid "Oriel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:693
msgid "A courtier's chest, sold for his gambling debts. Three from the Locking's deck: {clue}. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:694
msgid "The cards chose this one for you, dear. {clue}. A {colour} chest: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:695
msgid "The court's cartomancer. She draws three cards from the Locking's own deck for each chest: a suit drawn twice is what the ward holds (Coins, Swords for weapons, Mantles for cloaks, Cups for potions, Wands for spells, Stars for gems); three different suits, and nothing's warded. Prices by colour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:698
msgid "The cards are never wrong."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:698
msgid "As it was foretold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:699
msgid "The cards say I'm wanted elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:700
msgid "The cards did say you might."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:700
msgid "As you wish, dear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:701
msgid "I didn't see that coming. How rare."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:701
msgid "Oh!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:702
msgid "The cards warned me about you. Half again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:706
msgid "Silas Gilt"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:706
msgid "Silas"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:709
msgid "Out of the Maw's hoard, friend, through a crack in the Gate. I'm leaving town tonight, so {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:710
msgid "Hoard goods, very rare. Gold and gems, every one of them. For you, just {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:711
msgid "A fence for the Maw's hoard. He knows exactly what's in his chests, because he packed the demon gold himself: gilded iron sold as gold and gems, cheap. What's real comes cheap; the fakes are worth nothing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:713
msgid "Wonderful! No refunds."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:713
msgid "A pleasure. I really must be going."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:714
msgid "Can't stay. People to avoid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:715
msgid "Your loss, friend. Your very great loss."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:715
msgid "Suit yourself. I was never here."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:716
msgid "Easy, friend! Easy."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:716
msgid "Whoa there."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:717
msgid "Easy, friend! That'll cost a little extra."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:721
msgid "Old Aldo"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:721
msgid "Aldo"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:724
msgid "From an old house with a great many cellars. I've no idea what's in it. You tell me, and whatever you say it holds is my price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:725
msgid "Old things from an old house. Name what's inside: that's the price. Name it truly and I'll take a quarter off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:726
msgid "A tired old man in a plain cloak, with a very fine ring. He doesn't know what's in his chests: his price is whatever your slip says. Read it exactly and he takes a quarter off; read it wrong and you pay what it really holds, and a quarter more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:729
msgid "Well. We shall see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:729
msgid "Hm. Let's see what you heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:730
msgid "I'm needed elsewhere. Another day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:731
msgid "Another day, then. I'll be back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:731
msgid "Hm. A careful one. Good."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:732
msgid "Steady. It's older than both of us."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:732
msgid "Oh my."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:733
msgid "Steady! That was my grandfather's. I'll want a little more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:737
msgid "Avarax, the Gilded Maw"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:737
msgid "the Maw"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:740
msgid "A trifle from my hoard. One coin. All I ask is that you open it here, where I can see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:741
msgid "One coin, little Keywright. And then everyone in this city will want twice as much today. Isn't that fun?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:742
msgid "The demon of greed himself, in a borrowed body dripping with rings. He sells a chest for one coin, but greed is catching: buy it, and everyone who comes to your counter after him that day asks twice as much."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:744
msgid "Yesss."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:744
msgid "Open it. Let me see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:745
msgid "I have all the time in the world. You don't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:746
msgid "Clever little thing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:746
msgid "Mm. Another day, then. There are so many days."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:747
msgid "Careful. I break things too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:747
msgid "Ha."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:748
msgid "Careful. Greed always wants more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:761
msgid "Gods! It just... burst open! Keep the singing thing, then. The rest is going home with me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:766
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} and {1}"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Shop.cs:14
msgid "Bram's Stall"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Shop.cs:17 scripts/Core/Upgrades.cs:56
msgid "The Royal Emporium"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Shop.cs:752
msgid "Fished it out of the millpond this morning. I didn't shake it, it might break! Is {price} okay?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:51
msgid "Mara, the last archmage of the Keyhold, and Bram's old partner. She's hunted the Aldric Key for twenty years."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:52
msgid "The Crown Chest. The King gives it to you: it's yours by right. Open it, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:60 scripts/Ui/NotebookView.cs:283
msgid "Mara"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:61
msgid "King Aldric"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:70
#, csharp-format
msgid "Good evening. {0}, Collector for the Gilded Guild. Every Keywright in Aldmark pays the Guild a tithe, to keep the Gate. Your uncle never paid a penny."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:71
msgid "Twenty years I opened chests for folk who couldn't afford a Guild Keywright! For pennies!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:72
#, csharp-format
msgid "Twenty years of tithe, Bram: {0}. The Guild will be reasonable. {1} payments, one a week, starting small: {2}, {3} nights from now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:73
msgid "Miss one, and the Guild seals the stall. Good evening, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:74
msgid "Every fifth night, then. Don't look like that: a good ear pays any debt. We'll talk in the morning."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:90
#, csharp-format
msgid "Another season at the crossroads, {0}. The Guild hasn't come sniffing yet. Let's make the most of it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:91
#, csharp-format
msgid "There you are, {0}! My mark's faded, but look at your hand: it's yours now. And so is the stall."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:92
msgid "Folk bring us chests nobody else can open. You buy one, it opens for you, and you sell what's inside. So listen before you buy: that's the whole trade."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:96
msgid "You've a right to know what these chests are. Three hundred years ago the Maw, Avarax, ruled this realm through its gold. Every coin was his eye."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:98
msgid "King Aldric and the archmages locked every treasure away and chained the Maw behind the Gilded Gate. The Locking, they called it. The chests are what's left."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:100
msgid "And this is my one secret: a shard of the Aldric Key, broken in four when the Locking was made. It's yours now. Don't let the Guild see it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:102
msgid "So you're Bram's kin. You have the mark, and his ear for a chest, they say. I have something your uncle has wanted for twenty years. Find me what I ask for, and it's yours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:107
msgid "That's... a second shard. Where did she get it? Never mind. Never mind!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:108
msgid "That woman in the hood. I know that voice. Hear her out."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:110
msgid "My name is Mara. I was the last archmage of the Keyhold. Your uncle and I found the first shard together, a long time ago."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:112
msgid "The whole Key opens the Crown Chest: King Aldric's own, with the heart of the Locking inside. The Guild doesn't want your gold. It wants that chest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:114
msgid "Every tithe the Guild takes goes down through the Gilded Gate. The Maw is buying his way out, a coin at a time. And every chest you open loosens the Locking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:117
#, csharp-format
msgid "And that old fellow at the Emporium, the one with the ring? Look at the seal on it, {0}. That's the King. He's been testing you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:118
msgid "The King knows. He's looking for a Keywright he can trust with the Crown Chest. Be that Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:120
msgid "Vane's been asking about the shards. Whatever he offers you tonight, think hard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:123
msgid "The tithe is paid. But the Gate is hungry, and the Guild has decided you owe it something for its patience."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:124
msgid "They'll keep coming, and every week they'll want twice as much. Let's see how long we can make them wait."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:135
msgid "Bram's welcome"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:136
msgid "Bram's secret"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:138
msgid "The Guild's terms"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:143
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} Bring me {1} {2}, and the next shard is yours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:143 scripts/Ui/NotebookView.cs:363
msgid "this week"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:143
msgid "before the Guild comes again"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:153
#, csharp-format
msgid "A note from the Hooded Woman: \"{0}\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:155
msgid "A note from the Hooded Woman: \"You gave them the shards. Now the Guild will have the Crown Chest. Pay your debt: it's all you have left.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:157
msgid "The last week of the tithe, and it's already paid: nobody's coming for anything this week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:158
msgid "The debt's last week. Pay this, and the stall is yours. Truly yours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:164
msgid "Something enchanted. The last shard was hidden with magic, and only magic will find it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:167
msgid "A spellbook. The Keyhold wrote down where it hid every shard, in spells only a Keyhold book can hold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:168
msgid "A gem. The Key was set with them, and they remember where the rest of it went."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:169
msgid "Old coin. The Key-smiths were paid in it, and every coin was stamped with where they worked."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:170
msgid "A blade. The Wardens who carried the shards away were buried with their swords."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:175
msgid "Good. Here: the second shard. Don't let the Guild see it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:176
msgid "The third shard. One more, and the Key is whole."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:177
msgid "The last shard. Bram will know what to do with it. So will I."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:183
#, csharp-format
msgid "Before you pay. The Guild knows about the Key. {0}, I hear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:184
msgid "Give them to me, and the Guild will forget half of tonight's tithe. Generous, no?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:187
msgid " shard"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:187
msgid " shards"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:191
msgid "A sensible choice. The Guild remembers its friends. So does its master."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:192
msgid "Pity. The Guild remembers that too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:199
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} week early"
msgid_plural "{0} weeks early"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:200
msgid "Before I've even come for it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:204
#, csharp-format
msgid "All of it? Now? {0}. Then the Guild... has no further claim on Bram's stall."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:205
msgid "Free and clear, and ahead of time! Twenty years, and the stall is ours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:210
msgid "Free and clear! Twenty years, and the stall is ours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:214
msgid "And the Guild has the shards. Somewhere under the palace, they're looking for the Crown Chest. Let them look."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:216
#, csharp-format
msgid "And we've {0} of the Key's {1} shards. Mara will keep asking: keep trading, and we may find the Crown Chest yet."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:218
msgid "The Crown Chest can wait. The Key's not going anywhere, and neither are we."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:225
msgid "Bram. It's been a long time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:226
msgid "Mara. The Key. You found all of it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:227
msgid "Your kin did the finding. And the King has come himself, with the Crown Chest. Quickly: the Guild is a day behind us."
